    </credit>
  </info>

  <title>Data import</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Administration</gui><gui>Data</gui><gui>Data
  import</gui></guiseq> reads contacts or products from an .xls spreadsheet.
  The file must have the columns, in the order, that <link
  xref="data_export"/> writes; export a few first and use that file as the
  pattern. Choose the file under <gui>Import contacts</gui> or <gui>Import
  products</gui>. If its columns do not match, a message says so.</p>

  <section id="contacts">
  <title>Importing contacts</title>
  <p>The contacts in the file are listed. Check or clear
  <gui>Customer</gui>, <gui>Vendor</gui>, <gui>Employee</gui> and
  <gui>Service provider</gui> on each, and right click any you do not want
  and choose <gui>Delete contact</gui>. Choose the <gui>Markup :</gui> and
  <gui>Terms :</gui> they all get, and click <gui>Import</gui>. Each contact is
  also added to every <link xref="mailing_lists">mailing list</link> marked
  <gui>Auto add</gui>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="products">
  <title>Importing products</title>
  <p>The products in the file are listed. Check or clear <gui>Sellable</gui>,
  <gui>Purchasable</gui>, <gui>Manufactured</gui>, <gui>Job</gui> and
  <gui>Stock</gui> on each, and right click any you do not want and choose
  <gui>Delete product</gui>. Choose the <gui>Revenue account :</gui>,
  <gui>Expense account :</gui> and <gui>Tax rate :</gui> they all get, and
  click <gui>Import</gui>.</p>
  <p>Barcodes from another program often clash with the ones PyGtk Posting
  makes. <gui>Barcode tool</gui> can put letters in front of every imported
  barcode with <gui>Prepend</gui>, or <gui>Just generate the barcodes when
  importing</gui>.</p>
  </section>

</page>
